📡 8/23 Evening Update: Big Pie’s “ceasefire” over the weekend—waiting patiently for $80k before Jackson Hole—next week is the turning point 🧘

The weekend market was dull. Big Pie traded in a tight range around $77,565, oscillating between $75.5K and $77.7K within the day—no clear direction, just waiting. $ETH  also stabilized near the $2,466 level.

Why has it been so “grinding” lately?
🔹 After a one-week surge of 23%, longs need to rest and profit-taking has to be digested—this is normal consolidation during strong runs;
🔹 The triple positives (Treasury buybacks/Trump-friendly stance/SEC easing) have already been mostly priced in, so the short-term lacks fresh catalysts;
🔹 The real “starting gun” hasn’t fired yet—the closer Jackson Hole (8/27–29) is approaching, and big players are holding back, waiting for the shoe to drop.

Next week (8/24–29) is the decision week:
🔸 Once Jackson Hole kicks off: if it turns dovish → Big Pie surges toward $80k and opens up new room; if it’s vague/unclear → a pullback to fill gaps at high levels;
🔸 Key levels: $78–80K above is the breakout target; $75K / $73.5K below are pullback supports;
🔸 Strategy: don’t panic or chase until the consolidation breaks—leave the direction for next week. For a breakout, follow; for a pullback, consider only after stabilization. Don’t bet on $80k ahead of time.

The weekend is a day to rest, and the chart is resting too. Next week’s Jackson Hole—do you think Big Pie will break above $80k, or pull back first? Let’s discuss in the comments 👇

